  "description": "A persistent conversational unit built on exact holograms, created empty from a design you choose and taught from your own text; the package ships no voice and no text. Its alphabet is Prism's 320 tokens (characters, common words and chat tags) plus subwords you can mint from your own text. It learns every exchange it hears and says, plus anything taught or ingested by reference, into exact per-conversation counts for the context lengths you pick. Memory grows with the text learned (ModelDesign.Estimate gives the cost by formula). It has a conversation memory for long matches (its trust can be calibrated on your own text and is journaled) and an optional learned sharing layer (token classes and solved trust) that learns only when you call LearnStep, with Compare scoring held-out text with and without it; it offers N sampled replies to pick from without learning anything; takes bounded and fading approve or disapprove feedback without touching memory; forgets a conversation exactly; and rebuilds its whole state bit for bit from its journal on a HoloDb page store, including after a crash. Every choice can be inspected per context length.",
